examples.question_text:
Write the domain and range of the graph in inequality and interval notation.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black,->] (-3,0)--(4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-2)--(0,4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,thick] (-2,-1)--(3,3);
\fill[black] (-2,-1) circle (2pt);
\fill[black] (3,3) circle (2pt);
\path (-2,-1) node[below left] {$(-2,-1)$} (3,3) node[above left] {$(3,3)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
The shadow on the $x$-axis extends from $-2$ to $3$. Both endpoints are included.

Domain: $-2\leq x\leq3$, or $[-2,3]$.

The shadow on the $y$-axis extends from $-1$ to $3$, including both boundaries.

Range: $-1\leq y\leq3$, or $[-1,3]$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{shadow}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,->] (-3,0)--(4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-2)--(0,4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,thick] (-2,-1)--(3,3);
\fill[black] (-2,-1) circle (2pt);
\fill[black] (3,3) circle (2pt);
\path (-2,-1) node[below left] {$(-2,-1)$} (3,3) node[above left] {$(3,3)$};
\draw[shadow,dashed,thick] (-2,0)--(3,0);
\draw[shadow,dashed,thick] (0,-1)--(0,3);
\foreach \p in {(-2,0),(3,0),(0,-1),(0,3)} \fill[shadow] \p circle (2pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

